slam-rs JSON inputs: dataset VIO configurations and RoboCap calibration.

Each dataset in ../slam.toml selects one configuration. euroc_config.json is
msdmg_config.json with EuRoC's sensor facts only: no fisheye mask (safe radius
0 on a pinhole rig) and RootSLAM's EuRoC recall patch norms. tumvi_config.json
is msdmg_config.json with TUM-VI's 40 px detection grid and 320 px fisheye mask
(docs/reproduce.md lists what is carried from RootSLAM's config). The
reference profile leaves it unchanged. The default fast profile applies the
three keys in profiles/fast.json. profiles/live.json is the RoboCap live
profile (robocap-live's default): the fast keys plus a deferred keyframe solve
(port.keyframe_solve_deferred, D84) and 5 LM iterations. profiles/live30.json
adds a 70 px detection grid (about 40 % less frontend work; outside the 10 s
clip's ATE band, inside the full session's). Both live profiles set
backend.mode to realtime: when backend.enabled turns the persistent map on, it
runs on its own thread and tracking never waits for it; reference and fast keep
the offline default (inline, repeatable). profiles/rootslam-parity.json is the
fast keys plus RootSLAM's values of the backend.loop_closing knobs (camera-0
query, raw BRIEF tests, OpenGV's RANSAC schedule capped at 35 draws, inlier
ratio 0, I6 pose-graph edges), for parity checks against RootSLAM runs only.
It keeps the bug fixes (B3, B4, B8 and the others), so it reproduces
RootSLAM's verification gates, not its candidate supply: compare loop counts
per revisit window, not totals. The k1 A/B (DESIGN §4: fast plus one knob at
its parity value, MG, Offline, run-to-run band 0) moved one default: B5 queries
camera 0 only (MG with loops: final 2.458 vs 2.599 cm, +LC 4.929 vs 4.946 cm).
B1, B12 and B15 keep the fixed value; B16 keeps it for lack of runs. RootSLAM's
TUM-VI loop gates (20 / 30 inliers) regress MG and are not applied anywhere.
tests/test_config_profiles.py checks overlays
and rejects unknown keys. tests/test_reference.py checks that every named
configuration parses.

The RoboCap block selects msdmo_config.json and
robocap_calib_downscale3.json. The latter describes the four selected cameras
at one-third resolution. slam_rs.tracking.check_calibration_matches_recording
compares its intrinsics, extrinsics, distortion, and IMU model with the catalog
feed before tracking.
